# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Files that must NEVER enter version control.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The real credentials file. This is the single most important line here:
# committing .env would leak the institution's TikTok API secret.
.env

# Collected research data. Excluded for two reasons:
#   1. Ethics - the dataset contains personal data (usernames, comment text)
#      and must live only on approved storage, not on a code host.
#   2. Reproducibility - the code reproduces the data; the data is an output.
# Recursive (**) so this also covers data/archive/<run>/raw_posts.csv and
# similar nested outputs, not just the top-level files.
data/**/*.csv
data/**/*.txt
logs/*.log

# Same reasoning applies to per-run archives and their derived summaries
# under analysis/ - only the reusable scripts and methodology notes (.py,
# .md) are safe to commit; the data itself and any text derived from it stay
# local. Logs under analysis/ carry the same per-post usernames the top-level
# logs/*.log rule protects against, so they're excluded too.
analysis/**/*.csv
analysis/**/*.txt
analysis/**/*.log

# Keep the empty directories themselves in the repository so that a fresh
# clone has the correct structure before the first run.
!data/.gitkeep
!logs/.gitkeep

# Standard Python artefacts.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/

# Visual Studio IDE cache (not part of the project).
.vs/
